.TH IMUD 8 "2026-08-05" "imud 1.8.2" "System Manager's Manual"
.SH NAME
imud \- IMU daemon for marine and robotics navigation
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B imud
[\fB\-\-config\fR \fIPATH\fR]
[\fB\-\-replay\fR \fIFILE\fR]
[\fB\-\-skip\-bias\-cal\fR]
[\fB\-\-no\-nmea\fR]
[\fB\-\-no\-highrate\fR]
[\fB\-\-foreground\fR]
[\fB\-\-version\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B imud
reads from an IMU (gyroscope + accelerometer) and a magnetometer over I2C,
fuses the sensor data with a Multiplicative Extended Kalman Filter (MEKF),
and publishes attitude estimates in several optional formats:
.PP
.RS 4
\(bu\ \ NMEA 0183 sentences (UDP broadcast and/or a TCP listener, port 10110)
for chartplotters and autopilots
.br
\(bu\ \ High-rate binary packets (UDP port 10111) for machine-vision and ROS2
.br
\(bu\ \ The same binary packets over a local AF_UNIX subscription socket,
plus an optional TCP listener (port 10112) for remote consumers
.RE
.PP
By default only the local AF_UNIX stream socket is enabled; every network
output (NMEA UDP/TCP, high-rate UDP, stream TCP) is an explicit opt-in in
.IR imud.conf (5).
When magnetic declination is configured (via
.IR imud.conf (5)),
imud also emits true (geographic) heading in NMEA and the binary packet.
.PP
imud is normally run as a systemd service.
Use
.BR "systemctl enable --now imud"
after installation.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-config \ PATH
Load configuration from
.I PATH
instead of the default search path.
This replaces the search rather than heading it: if
.I PATH
does not exist, imud logs a warning and runs on built-in defaults \(em it does
not fall back to
.IR ~/.config/imud/imud.conf ,
so a mistyped path cannot silently start the daemon on a different
configuration.
.IP
Without
.BR \-\-config ,
the daemon searches
.I /etc/imud/imud.conf
and then
.IR ~/.config/imud/imud.conf ;
neither existing is not an error.
.TP
.BI \-\-replay \ FILE
Replay an .imucap capture (recorded by the [capture] black box, or a
synthetic scenario) through the full pipeline: both sensors are forced onto
the sim driver in playback mode.
Pacing and looping come from the [device] sim_* keys; see
.BR imud.conf (5)
and docs/capture.md.
.TP
.B \-\-skip\-bias\-cal
Skip the stationary gyro-bias estimation window at startup.
Useful when restarting quickly and the sensor has not moved since the
previous run.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-nmea
Disable the NMEA output stream regardless of the config file setting.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-highrate
Disable the high-rate binary output stream regardless of the config file
setting.
.TP
.B \-\-foreground
(Accepted but currently a no-op; imud does not daemonize.)
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version string and exit.
.SH SIGNALS
.TP
.B SIGHUP
Reload hot-reloadable configuration fields without restarting.
Hot fields include MEKF noise parameters, output rates, the stats heartbeat
rate, the log level, and the
.B [position]
declination inputs (declination_deg, lat_deg/lon_deg, wmm_file \(em the WMM
declination and field reference are recomputed, unless a live position
source owns them).
The log file, if configured, is reopened on reload so logrotate can rotate it.
If the reloaded file fails to parse, the current configuration is kept.
Fields marked
.B [restart]
in
.IR imud.conf (5)
require a full restart and are ignored during a reload.
.IP
The file re-read is the one the daemon actually loaded at startup, including
when that was the
.I ~/.config/imud/imud.conf
fallback.
A reload starts from the built-in defaults and then applies the file, exactly as
startup does, so removing a
.B [hot]
key from the file restores its default rather than leaving the running value in
place.
If the file has since been deleted, the running configuration is kept.
.TP
.BR SIGTERM ", " SIGINT
Graceful shutdown: flush output, join all threads, close hardware.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/imud/imud.conf
Default configuration file.
.TP
.I ~/.config/imud/imud.conf
Per-user configuration override.
.TP
.I /etc/imud/cal.json
Calibration data (hard/soft-iron offsets, gyro bias, accelerometer corrections).
Written by
.BR imud-cal (8).
.TP
.I /var/lib/imud/
Black-box capture files when [capture] is enabled; also the daemon's state
directory.
.TP
.I /usr/share/imud/WMM.COF
World Magnetic Model 2025 coefficient file (imud-wmm-data package).
Used for automatic magnetic-declination computation when
.B position.lat_deg
and
.B position.lon_deg
are set.
Valid 2025.0\(en2030.0.
An operator-supplied
.I /etc/imud/WMM.COF
overrides the packaged data when present.
.TP
.I /run/imud/imud.sock
Unix domain socket used by
.BR imud-status (1)
to query daemon health.
Mode 0660, owner
.IR imud:imud .
.TP
.I /usr/lib/udev/rules.d/60\-imud.rules
udev rule granting the
.I i2c
and
.I gpio
groups access to
.I /dev/i2c\-*
and
.IR /dev/gpiochip* .
Raspberry Pi OS ships equivalent rules in
.IR 99\-com.rules ;
this file is what makes a stock Debian install work.
A source install places it in
.IR /etc/udev/rules.d .
.SH USERS AND GROUPS
The daemon runs as the system user
.I imud
with primary group
.IR imud ,
which owns
.I /run/imud
and both Unix domain sockets.
Hardware access comes from the supplementary groups
.I gpio
.RI ( /dev/gpiochip* )
and
.I i2c
.RI ( /dev/i2c\-* ).
All three are created at install time if absent; the service refuses to start
without
.I gpio
and
.IR i2c .
.PP
To connect to the stream socket or run
.BR imud-status (1)
as an ordinary user, join the
.I imud
group \(em not
.I gpio
\(em with
.BR "adduser <user> imud" .
.SH SUPPORTED HARDWARE
.TP
IMUs
ISM330DHCX (ST), ICM-20948 (TDK)*, ICM-42688-P (TDK)*, LSM6DSO/LSM6DSOX (ST)*,
sim (software simulation)
.TP
Magnetometers
MMC5983MA (MEMSIC), AK09916 (via ICM-20948 I2C master)*, LIS3MDL (ST)*,
LIS2MDL (ST)*, sim
.PP
Drivers marked * are experimental: implemented but not yet validated on real
silicon; imud logs a warning at startup when one is selected.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B 0
on graceful shutdown,
.B 1
on configuration or hardware initialisation error, or if the
.B [stream]
output thread cannot be started \(em that stream is the one output a stock
daemon provides and every bridge reads it, so running without it would produce
nothing while reporting active.
The optional outputs
.RB ( [nmea] ,
.BR [highrate] ,
and the position thread)
warn and continue instead; whatever they had already bound is closed, so a
client is refused rather than left connected to a socket nobody is serving.
.SH EXAMPLES
Run in the foreground with the simulation driver:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
imud --config /etc/imud/imud.conf --no-nmea
.EE
.RE
.PP
Reload configuration at runtime:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
sudo systemctl reload imud
# or:
kill -HUP $(pidof imud)
.EE
.RE
